  "reference_solution": "WITH eligible AS (SELECT device_id,day,day-CAST(ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY device_id ORDER BY day) AS INTEGER) AS island FROM device_days WHERE online IS TRUE) SELECT device_id,MIN(day) AS start_day,MAX(day) AS end_day,COUNT(*) AS day_count FROM eligible GROUP BY device_id,island",
  "solution_explanation": "After retaining online dates, the difference between calendar date and row number is constant within a consecutive run. Partition independently per device.",
  "hints": [
    "An island requires both a device key and calendar adjacency.",
    "After filtering, gaps in dates must remain detectable.",
    "Derive an island key from ordered dates and a per-device sequence, then aggregate."
  ],
  "senior_review": "Distinguish missing telemetry from known uptime; document the inference and the uniqueness contract.",
